diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index d42f183b5a1e743490747fb0f843ecaf5f69a344..2dc1ce828c8c8019c97e6b8ec6f9ad8651651a42 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -19,0 +20,8 @@ All notable codex-tui changes are recorded here.
+- Preserve bounded stdio framing across cancellation and deliver the final closed-channel disconnect snapshot exactly once; retain timeout and fail-closed transport behavior.
+- Bound Registry/loaded-list pagination across bootstrap, hydration and reconciliation with cycle/no-progress, count, identity-byte and total-time budgets; preserve partial inventory without promoting it to complete authority.
+- Reject malformed or missing GitLab approval fields instead of treating unknown evidence as zero required approvals; preserve valid empty-rule and explicit server evidence semantics.
+- Locate exact transcript search hits beyond the first 200 items with a bounded global descending scan and scope-consistent continuation; report missing/deleted targets explicitly.
+- Retain kill-and-reap ownership through all fallible PTY startup phases and poll child completion from the existing detached actor; add stage-specific native failure injection.
+- Apply retained payload byte/count limits to queued RPC and pending user requests; quarantine overloaded sessions rather than dropping approvals or replaying mutations.
+- Add a five-case actual-binary stdio/EOF/cursor regression to the existing hosted PTY workflow, plus bilingual diagnostic and current-release wording updates. No Stable or real-environment qualification is implied.
+
diff --git a/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md b/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
index bceb6c4928386dba0ed5a275660b1e6465359f14..f111b2b6349821befb80103059145ef3b4498ac1 100644
--- a/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
+++ b/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
@@ -14,0 +15,4 @@ Run `codex-tui doctor codex` (optionally `--target NAME`). Check the real `codex
+Stdio fragments remain buffered across timer/command cancellation; a backend EOF delivers the final disconnected snapshot once. Repeated/cyclic cursors, stalled pagination and total budgets produce explicit incomplete inventory, never complete mutation authority. Search jumps locate the exact item within a bounded global-history scan and retain a continuation cursor of the same scope; deleted targets or exhausted budgets report failure instead of silently jumping elsewhere.
+
+RPC notifications retain at most 1024 messages and 16 MiB of accounted payload. Pending interactive requests are limited to 64, 256 KiB each and 4 MiB in aggregate. Pagination allows up to 1024 pages, 200,000 identities, 32 MiB of accounted identity storage and 120 seconds across the scan. These are payload/accounting limits, not certified process RSS. Overload terminates/quarantines the session visibly; it does not discard arbitrary approval messages or replay write RPCs. An ordinary 50k-row scan remains supported within these limits.
+
@@ -19,0 +24,2 @@ In the repository at issue: inspect `git remote -v` **privately**, run `codex-tu
+Malformed GitLab approval-state JSON or missing `rules`, `approvals_required` or `approved` fields are unknown evidence and block client-side merging. An explicit valid empty rules array is distinct from a missing array. These checks do not replace GitLab server protections.
+
@@ -29,0 +36,2 @@ Try the in-app `?` keymap: `t` opens the Drawer and `F6` (or `Ctrl+]`) returns f
+PTY children remain owned by a kill-and-reap guard through initialization and the detached actor lifetime. Failure to obtain the reader/writer, publish Ready or start the reader cannot abandon that ownership. Fault-injection tests exercise each startup stage using local children, not real SSH acceptance.
+
diff --git a/docs/implementation/v1.4-audit-closure.md b/docs/implementation/v1.4-audit-closure.md
index 38fa6db6e44834598660c5d877e530686ceaef4c..8bfe5cd94914bef6cad6494d31f84e65c24a1ace 100644
--- a/docs/implementation/v1.4-audit-closure.md
+++ b/docs/implementation/v1.4-audit-closure.md
@@ -3 +3 @@
-Baseline: `81a1725ca85b1028264f98427a57012077e794af`.
+Historical baseline: `81a1725ca85b1028264f98427a57012077e794af`. The 2026-10-11 reliability follow-up is based on `d1e4f8aadb2e1275e9e55ad51c8f7e50e6acd797`; current qualification must always be bound to the resulting exact source SHA, not either historical baseline.
@@ -28,3 +28 @@ receive process-unique revisions, and cold/revised renders format only the selec
-Existing v1.3/v1.4 module ceilings remain unchanged; extracted workers and diagnostics
-have their own ceilings. Legacy state migration, old Git parsing, protocol fallback,
-plan/confirm/receipt mutations and uncertain-outcome rules remain supported.
+The single v1.4 module ceiling ledger requires an explicit defect-maintenance review for touched or extracted modules. No parallel numeric ledger is introduced. Current Git compatibility, protocol fallback, plan/confirm/receipt mutations and uncertain-outcome rules remain supported. Undeployed legacy JSON/SQLite migration is not a requirement: first installation uses current SQLite v4 and refuses older or future schemas without destructive reset.
@@ -74,0 +73,6 @@ records whether ancestor-only proof was enabled plus the eligible prefixes.
+
+## 2026-10-11 reliability follow-up
+
+Maintenance-only changes preserve framing across cancellation, consume final disconnected snapshots exactly once, bound startup/hydration/reconciliation pagination, reject malformed GitLab approval evidence, and locate exact search hits with scope-consistent history cursors. PTY actor ownership spans every fallible initialization stage; RPC/pending-request and pagination identity payloads have count and byte budgets.
+
+Retained tests include actual RpcSession/WebSocket fixtures, deterministic stream cancellation, closed watch channels, approval parsing negatives, native PTY startup failure injection and an actual-binary isolated stdio/EOF/repeated-cursor harness. The canonical terminal regression workflow retains the five-case receipt and exact binary checksum. Tests and receipts are hosted-development evidence only; no real account, internal GitLab, SSH, multi-hour real-process certification, productivity ROI or Stable permission is inferred. Numerical render/soak results from an older SHA remain historical, not a qualification for modified code.
diff --git a/docs/release/install-upgrade.md b/docs/release/install-upgrade.md
index be7e6e67a116b7df34e065a508d6f3a71706f375..d9377672903b05eae3294b28a12ab3000ea42a9f 100644
--- a/docs/release/install-upgrade.md
+++ b/docs/release/install-upgrade.md
@@ -173 +173 @@ vX.Y.Z
-The first permitted stable product line is v1.0.0. Stable publication fails closed if any required evidence is absent. Both the supported `stable_publish.py` path and a direct `stable + publish=true` workflow dispatch require GitHub repository **release immutability** to be enabled and verifiable and require the canonical **main branch protection policy** to remain intact: strict canonical checks, each check pinned to the GitHub Actions App dynamically observed on the exact source SHA, administrator enforcement, force pushes disabled and branch deletion disabled. Direct workflow publication additionally requires repository secret `CODEX_TUI_ADMIN_READ_TOKEN` with fine-grained **Administration(read)** permission; absence, inaccessible administration state, app-source drift or policy drift is fail-closed. Preview and stable publish=false remain credential-free. Enable immutability before the v1.4 release. The setting protects future releases and does not retroactively make older releases immutable.
+The current candidate product line is v1.4.0; the historical v1.0.0 release is an audit record, not current-source qualification or permission to deploy. Stable publication fails closed if any required evidence is absent. Both the supported `stable_publish.py` path and a direct `stable + publish=true` workflow dispatch require GitHub repository **release immutability** to be enabled and verifiable and require the canonical **main branch protection policy** to remain intact: strict canonical checks, each check pinned to the GitHub Actions App dynamically observed on the exact source SHA, administrator enforcement, force pushes disabled and branch deletion disabled. Direct workflow publication additionally requires repository secret `CODEX_TUI_ADMIN_READ_TOKEN` with fine-grained **Administration(read)** permission; absence, inaccessible administration state, app-source drift or policy drift is fail-closed. Preview and stable publish=false remain credential-free. Enable immutability before the v1.4 release. The setting protects future releases and does not retroactively make older releases immutable.
diff --git a/docs/zh-CN/guides/troubleshooting.md b/docs/zh-CN/guides/troubleshooting.md
